{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-action-strategy", "file": "references/demo-request-information-gate.md", "content": "# Information gate for costly demo requests

In capped-cost ARC streams, a demo request spends one point just like an incorrect submission. Treat it as an experiment, not as a default continuation.

Before requesting, record internally:
- the unresolved, test-relevant question;
- at least two plausible hypotheses still consistent with all available demos;
- the specific observation in a new pair that would distinguish them;
- why that information is worth the request cost relative to a submission.

If no meaningful competing hypotheses or discriminating observation can be named, do not request yet. Analyze all received pairs first: enumerate changed and unchanged cells/objects, test candidate rules against both, and update the hypothesis ledger. After a demo arrives, perform that delta analysis before any further action; never issue consecutive requests without intervening reasoning. Stop requesting once the new evidence no longer changes the candidate rule or the remaining uncertainty is not test-relevant.

This gate complements the main continual-ARC action procedure; it does not require certainty before requesting, only a concrete, worthwhile experiment.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792545531/attempts/bc528d856f1a41f1a28c3fa14e5fbbd6/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzles/continual-arc-action-strategy/references/demo-request-information-gate.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-action-strategy", "file": "references/post-rejection-exact-grid-audit.md", "content": "# Exact-grid audit after rejection

A wrong submission only rejects the complete candidate; it does not say which cell or sub-rule failed. Before another request or submission, inspect the exact action JSON that was sent, reconstruct its cellwise delta from the original test input, and replay the implementation against every demo. Do not regenerate the candidate from an informal rule summary or rely on memory for sparse marker coordinates. Check row/column indexing, source marker transcription, additions and salient unchanged alignments, then separate selector/geometry uncertainty from serialization mistakes. Only after this audit decide whether a new demo discriminates named alternatives or a materially different candidate is justified. Avoid arbitrary distance cutoffs and near-duplicate guesses unsupported by the demos.

This lesson is especially relevant when grids are sparse and a small coordinate transcription error changes many projected/fill cells.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792545531/attempts/bc528d856f1a41f1a28c3fa14e5fbbd6/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzles/continual-arc-action-strategy/references/post-rejection-exact-grid-audit.md"}
